%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:tahoe -- Tahoe drops the window to one segment at a fast retransmit, and turns SACK off.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; TcpTahoe has no fast
recovery, and "an algorithm without SACK recovery turns sackSupport off".

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms. This test separates TcpTahoe: TcpNewReno, TcpReno, TcpCubic and DcTcp offer SACK, TcpVegas
and TcpWestwood keep more than one segment at a fast retransmit, and TcpNoCongestionControl
and DumbTcp have no window.

Host under test: host1, with sackSupport true (the default), which sends 100000 bytes; the
round trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the 15th data segment once. Observation: level 1, the
SYN of host1 has no SACK-Permitted option; level 2, the smallest window is one MSS, 1460
bytes, without a timeout.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: tahoe
%# value: "TcpTahoe"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassTahoe")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return tcpOptionCount(context.event.packet, inet::tcp::TCPOPTION_SACK_PERMITTED) == 0; })
             .describe("the SYN of host1, without SACK-Permitted")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                                        .captureMin("smallestCwnd", "value")
                                        .within(4.0)))
        .meanwhile(never(on("host1.tcp").signal("numRtos").describe("a retransmission timeout").within(4.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 100000")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("{smallestCwnd} == 1460")
             .describe("the ACK of the last byte; the smallest window was one MSS")
             .within(6.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassTahoe compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpTahoe"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassTahoe: PASS
